1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,358
There's a conversation we have to finish.

2
00:00:04,358 --> 00:00:10,434
What was it about?

3
00:00:10,434 --> 00:00:12,512
It was about caring.

4
00:00:12,512 --> 00:00:12,712
Oh?

5
00:00:12,712 --> 00:00:13,112
Yes, caring.

6
00:00:13,112 --> 00:00:15,850
I said that it makes me feel good

7
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:17,868
that you care about Michelle.

8
00:00:17,868 --> 00:00:19,504
Well, I do care about Michelle.

9
00:00:19,504 --> 00:00:22,560
And it makes me feel good that you care about me.

10
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:25,324
You know I do.

11
00:00:25,324 --> 00:00:29,780
You're a ... wonderful friend.

12
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:33,941
And it makes me feel good

13
00:00:33,941 --> 00:00:38,714
that you care about us.

14
00:00:38,714 --> 00:00:39,834
Well ... well,

15
00:00:39,834 --> 00:00:41,692
I do, Harry.

16
00:00:41,692 --> 00:00:44,669
It's only natural that if I care about Michelle

17
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:46,669
and I care about you,

18
00:00:46,669 --> 00:00:49,361
then I care about us.

19
00:00:49,361 --> 00:00:50,839
It's OK, Susan.

20
00:00:50,839 --> 00:00:52,339
We had this part of the conversation

21
00:00:52,339 --> 00:00:53,936
before Michelle and her friends arrived.

22
00:00:53,936 --> 00:00:55,603
Now comes the good part.

23
00:00:55,603 --> 00:00:56,581
Like what?

24
00:00:56,581 --> 00:01:01,174
Well, assume that if you care about Michelle

25
00:01:01,174 --> 00:01:02,537
and you care about me

26
00:01:02,537 --> 00:01:04,680
and you care about us,

27
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:07,755
that we can talk about us.

28
00:01:07,755 --> 00:01:11,471
I mean--you and me.

29
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:14,449
Isn't that right?

30
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:20,405
What are you trying to say, Harry?

31
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:23,383
What I'm trying to say ...

32
00:01:23,383 --> 00:01:29,339
since this is so easy ....

33
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:53,163
Here are ten letters that express my feelings for you.

34
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:54,763
Don't be silly, Harry.

35
00:01:54,763 --> 00:01:57,140
You want a hint?

36
00:01:57,140 --> 00:01:58,140
It's two words.

37
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:00,451
You're making the game harder.

38
00:02:00,451 --> 00:02:03,696
Can't you figure it out?

39
00:02:03,696 --> 00:02:05,322
Seven letters ... two words ...

40
00:02:05,322 --> 00:02:09,052
that express the feelings that I feel for you in my heart.

41
00:02:09,052 --> 00:02:28,898
Harry, I get it! Harry

42
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:31,876
Well? Does that mean you'll marry me?

43
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:41,810
Is that a proposal, or are we just playing a game?

44
00:02:41,810 --> 00:02:47,160
Sit down, Susan.

45
00:02:47,160 --> 00:03:07,612
There's something I have to ask you.

46
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:09,945
Susan, will you marry me?

47
00:03:09,945 --> 00:03:12,069
It's such an important decision.

48
00:03:12,069 --> 00:03:14,900
There's so many things to talk about.

49
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:19,523
There are three things that have to be done first, Harry.

50
00:03:19,523 --> 00:03:20,923
Three things?

51
00:03:20,923 --> 00:03:24,421
First, we have to decide where to live.

52
00:03:24,421 --> 00:03:25,161
Well, that's easy.

53
00:03:25,161 --> 00:03:26,229
We talked about that earlier.

54
00:03:26,229 --> 00:03:27,479
We'll live in New York.

55
00:03:27,479 --> 00:03:28,886
All right.

56
00:03:28,886 --> 00:03:29,314
Second,

57
00:03:29,314 --> 00:03:34,413
we have to talk to Michelle together about being married.

58
00:03:34,413 --> 00:03:36,693
We'll do that immediately.

59
00:03:36,693 --> 00:03:37,391
What's the third thing?

60
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:40,369
You have to ask for my father's permission.

61
00:03:40,369 --> 00:03:42,689
Absolutely!

62
00:03:42,689 --> 00:03:44,043
But first things first.

63
00:03:44,043 --> 00:03:46,325
We have to go pick up Michelle.

64
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:52,281
Oh, I'm so happy, Harry!

65
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:55,281
Not as happy as I am.
